.TH CRUSH 1 "August 2026" "Cruine 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cru crush \- interactive shell over the cruine command tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cru crush
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B cru sh
.RB [ \-p " path" ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-color ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cru crush
opens a stateful REPL that navigates the cruine command tree. Commands are
resolved relative to the current tree path, so the shell behaves like a
filesystem over the command hierarchy. The prompt reflects the current
path, e.g.
.B cru/b> .
.PP
The initial path may be given positionally
.RB ( "cru crush a/analyze" )
or with
.BR \-p/\-\-path .
An unknown start path is reported but does not prevent the shell from
opening.
.PP
On interactive terminals readline provides tab completion over built-ins,
command names, aliases, and flags, plus persistent history in
.BR ~/.cru_history .
.SH BUILT-INS
.TP
.B exit ", " quit
Leave the shell.
.TP
.B cd " [path]"
Change the current tree path. With no argument, return to the root.
.TP
.B pwd
Print the current path as
.IR cru/<group>/<command> .
.TP
.B ls
List the children (commands and aliases) of the current node.
.TP
.B tree " [path]"
Print a depth-limited subtree rooted at the current node or the given path.
.TP
.B help " [path]"
Print detailed help for the current node or the given path, including
built-ins and hints.
.TP
.B clear
Clear the terminal.
.SH PATH SYNTAX
.TP
.B ~ ", " /
Reset to the tree root.
.TP
.B .
Current node (no-op).
.TP
.B ..
Move up one level; at the root it is a no-op.
.TP
.I child/child
Slash-separated relative descent, e.g.
.BR cd b/bundle .
.PP
Any line that is not a built-in is split with
.B shlex
and dispatched as a tree command relative to the current path, so
.B bake
at
.B cru/b>
runs
.BR "cru b/bake" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p,\ \-\-path " PATH"
Initial tree path.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors in the prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ~/.cru_history
Command history; written on exit when the shell runs on a terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cru (1),
.BR rc.json (5)
